  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Observe that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies on the given ellipse.</p><p>Equation of tangent to the ellipse at the given point is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Equation of normal passing through same point will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>36</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Now tangent and normal&nbsp;intersects the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of circle with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;as diameter will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#8658;</mtext><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>&nbsp;intersects the circle.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now let us find the equation of tangents to the circle at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>44</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>From&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>18</mn><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>304</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence this is the required option.</p></blockquote>",
